  "summary": "A multistage vertical turbine (diffuser) pump installed inside a pressurised suction can (barrel). Suction and discharge both connect to the head at grade; the liquid fills the can, flows down outside the column and bowls and enters the first-stage impeller at the bottom. Because the first stage sits well below grade, the static liquid height in the can adds to NPSH available — the main reason to choose a can pump for liquids near their boiling point.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Rotodynamic (centrifugal), diffuser type",
    "configuration": "Vertically suspended, double casing (can), multistage",
    "api_610_type": "VS6 (double-casing diffuser, vertically suspended)"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "stages": 4,
    "can": "Fabricated barrel with dished bottom, flanged to head",
    "shaft_seal": "Cartridge mechanical seal",
    "driver": "Vertical motor with thrust bearing; adjustable spacer coupling",
    "note": "Lengths shortened for display."
  },
